    "created_at": "2021-04-17T06:53:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-17T06:53:42Z",
    "body": "> `error for object 0x1: pointer being realloc'd was not allocated`\r\n\r\nOh yeah, *that's* bad. Looks like someone is trying to reallocate on a NULL pointer.\r\n\r\nWithout more information, I think it's really hard to debug this---is it from our code resulting from a compiler bug? (AFAIK the only unsafe we use is on Windows). Is it from a dependency of ours? Does it originate from Rust code or a C library like libgit2?\r\n\r\nI'll leave this issue open for now in case it happens again or someone else can reproduce it. If we don't see it again for a few months, we'll probably (unfortunately) have to close since we can't reproduce.\r\n\r\nThanks for letting us know!",
