    "updated_at": "2024-11-05T12:10:05Z",
    "body": "Just a heads up that I've noticed something similar recently in my shell and I wasn't sure why...\r\n\r\n```\r\ngit(59115,0x1ff4b7840) malloc: *** error for object 0x1: pointer being freed was not allocated\r\ngit(59115,0x1ff4b7840) malloc: *** set a breakpoint in malloc_error_break to debug\r\n```\r\n\r\nI presumed it was Starship but to be honest I don't know why considering I've not touched my config in a very long time. So it makes me think something I've added into my zshrc has caused the issue (but what I don't know).\r\n\r\nFor anyone interested, this is my zshrc:\r\nhttps://github.com/Integralist/dotfiles/blob/main/.zshrc\r\n\r\nUsually, it's small changes I make. I think the only \"meaty\" change I've made in recent times is using a simple lock mechanism to prevent multiple shells from trying to run conflicting operations like `brew_update`, `go_update` and `rust_update` when my terminal ([warp.dev](https://www.warp.dev/)) restarts (as it will open up all my old tabs, and each individual shell will otherwise attempt to call those shell functions):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/Integralist/dotfiles/blob/fa44e4d/.zshrc#L743-L809",
